  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australian Centre for International Agricultural Research: Contributions to International Agricultural Research Centres</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Australian Centre for International Agricultural Research (ACIAR) engages with and supports a range of other international agricultural research centres, institutes and associations as a valued donor and a research partner through establishing active working relationships and providing timely and consistent funding which contributes to addressing shared global challenges affecting our food and natural resource systems. These include direct engagement with the Asia Pacific Association of Agricultural Research Institutions (APAARI), Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN), CABI (an intergovernmental, not-for-profit organisation), International Centre for Insect Physiology and Ecology (icipe), Canada&apos;s International Development Research Centre (IDRC), The Pacific Community (SPC), World Bank, and the World Vegetable Center (WorldVeg).</narrative>
  </description>
